<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The prayer card's live clock leaf, LATIN digits (the default).

  Hosted inside the Glance composition through AndroidRemoteViews, so the
  launcher's own TextClock ticks the clock: no widget update, no alarm and no
  Doze grant can make it lag (brief P1 — the baked string could sit minutes
  behind after Doze).

  THE FORMATS ARE BAKED INTO THE LAYOUT, NOT SET AT RUNTIME. This is the fix
  for «لا یمكن تحمیل التطبيق المصغّر» / "Problem loading widget" measured on
  the POCO X7 Pro (HyperOS, Android 16, 2026-11-04): the launcher replaces
  TextClock with its own HomeMIUIWidgetTextClock, and
  RemoteViews.setString(id, "setFormat12Hour", ...) resolves the method with
  java.lang.String. The real signature is setFormat12Hour(CharSequence), so
  RemoteViews.getMethod threw ActionException inside RemoteViews.apply() and
  AppWidgetHostView swapped in its error view. No reflection setter can be
  made safe against a host-supplied subclass, so the 12/24 choice and the
  fa/latin digit choice are now four INFLATE-TIME layouts and the composition
  only sets colour, size and the click intent.

  BOTH format attributes carry the same pattern on purpose: the app's own
  12/24 setting must win over the system's, and setting the "other" one to
  null through a reflection setter is exactly what used to crash. The 24-hour
  variant is this file; widget_prayer_clock_12.xml is the 12-hour one.

  The click intent is set on the TextClock view itself (setOnClickPendingIntent
  from PrayerRemoteLeaves), so the clock still opens the app.
-->
<FrameLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content">

    <TextClock
        android:id="@+id/prayer_clock"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_gravity="center"
        android:contentDescription="ساعت"
        android:fontFamily="@font/calibri"
        android:fontFeatureSettings="tnum"
        android:format12Hour="HH:mm"
        android:format24Hour="HH:mm"
        android:includeFontPadding="false"
        android:maxLines="1"
        android:textLocale="en_US"
        android:textStyle="bold" />
</FrameLayout>
